==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{compound|name|sake|lang=en}}. From the phrase "(one's) [[name]]'s [[sake]]"; first recorded in the mid-seventeenth century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|nāmʹsāk}}, {{IPA|/ˈneɪmseɪk/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-namesake.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who is [[name]]d after another or for whom another is named.<!--the original sense-->
# A person with the same name as another.
# A ship or a building that is named after someone or something

====Synonyms====
* [[eponym]]

